{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-13T16:05:41.631Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 is complete.\n\nSummary of what I did:\n\n- **`src/kernel/languages/presets.ts`** (new): `LANGUAGE_PRESETS` (name, manifests, lock files, extensions) and `LANGUAGE_COVERAGE` (name, kind, covers) as data in the spec's order, plus `uncoveredBy(language)` returning `{ gates, extras }`, each in list order. Exported functions carry `@scenario languages: ...` and `@adr 017`.\n- **`src/kernel/languages/language-map.ts`** (new): pure `languageMap(paths)` — nearest manifest decides a path's language, `languages` in preset order, `languageOf` walks up from the path's folder — and async `readLanguageMap(projectRoot, config, extra)`, which lists tracked files via `lineEndings()` on `selectVcs` plus existing root manifests and `extra`, so `NoVcs` works. Imports only `selectVcs`, the `OsqConfig` type, node builtins, and `./presets.js`. No adapter, no `slice.ts`.\n- **`tests/languages-map.test.ts`** (new): plain `node:test` cases for every scenario/table row, with temp git projects (clean git env) and non-repo folders.\n- **`tests/import-graph.test.ts`** (edited, `tests.modify: true`): the `core stays inside core` rule now also allows resolved paths under `src/kernel`.\n\nVerification: task `verify` passes (4/4), and the proposal's `pnpm verify` passes (typechecks, build, full test suite, biome lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/184-language-gaps-reported/.run/results/1.md`."}}
